--- a well-formed GET
method -> GET
path -> /hello
version -> 1.1
query name -> ada
query n -> 42
header lookup is case-insensitive -> example.com
absent header takes the default -> -
a GET has an empty body, not a missing one -> b''
str(request) -> GET /hello HTTP/1.1
--- header names fold, values do not
name lowercased -> Example.COM
repeated field joined with a comma -> v1, v2
--- percent-decoding
path escape -> /a b/é
'+' is a space in a query -> a b
'+' is NOT a space in a path -> /a+b
escape in a query value -> /x
a valueless query key is empty -> 
--- the target forms a server must accept
absolute-form drops the authority -> /x
absolute-form with no path -> /
absolute-form with a query and no path -> 1
asterisk-form -> *
HTTP/1.0 needs no Host -> 1.0
a leading blank line is skipped -> GET
--- what must be refused
no Host on 1.1 -> 400 HTTP/1.1 request without a Host header
two Host headers -> 400 duplicate host header
two spaces in the request line -> 400 malformed request line
no version -> 400 malformed request line
not HTTP at all -> 400 unrecognised protocol in the request line
HTTP/2.0 over 1.1 framing -> 505 unsupported HTTP version '2.0'
space before the colon -> 400 malformed header name
obsolete line folding -> 400 obsolete line folding is not supported
a header line with no colon -> 400 malformed header line
a head that never ends -> 400 connection ended in the middle of the header block
nothing at all -> clean EOF
only blank lines -> 400 empty request line
a bad percent-escape -> 400 invalid percent-escape in the request target
a truncated percent-escape -> 400 truncated percent-escape in the request target
a fragment -> 400 a fragment must not be sent in a request target
a relative target -> 400 request target is not an absolute path
a bare LF inside a header value -> 400 malformed header value
a NUL inside a header value -> 400 malformed header value
a control character in the target -> 400 malformed request target
a header value that is not UTF-8 -> 400 bytes could not be decoded as UTF-8: invalid byte 0xff at position 0
a path that decodes to invalid UTF-8 -> 400 bytes could not be decoded as UTF-8: invalid byte 0xff at position 1
--- bounded, because the client chooses the size
a header block over 64 KiB -> 431 header block exceeded 65536 bytes
more than 100 header fields -> 431 more than 100 header fields
